  "steps": [
    "In a medium saucepan, combine the rinsed quinoa and beef broth. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer for 15 minutes until the liquid is absorbed and the quinoa is fluffy.",
    "While the quinoa cooks, heat the olive oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat. Add the diced bell pepper and red onion, sautéing for 4-5 minutes until the vegetables are softened and slightly browned.",
    "Add the lean ground beef to the skillet. Cook for 6-8 minutes, breaking the meat into small crumbles with a wooden spoon, until the beef is fully browned and reaches an internal temperature of 160°F (71°C).",
    "Stir the chili powder, cumin, garlic powder, salt, and drained black beans into the beef mixture. Cook for 2-3 minutes over medium heat until the beans are heated through and the spices are fragrant.",
    "Remove the quinoa from the heat and fluff with a fork. Divide the quinoa evenly among four bowls.",
    "Top each bowl with the beef and bean mixture, then sprinkle with crumbled feta cheese before serving."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Swap the beef broth for water if you prefer a milder flavor, but broth adds significant savory depth to the quinoa.",
    "For extra volume without many calories, stir in two cups of fresh baby spinach at the very end until wilted.",
    "If meal prepping, keep the feta in a separate small container to maintain its texture until you are ready to eat."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in airtight containers in the refrigerator for up to 4 days. Reheat in the microwave for 90 seconds.",
  "tools": [
